## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses practical iOS development skills, including Core Data modeling, SwiftUI data binding, secure encryption with CryptoKit, and fundamental testing practices.

## Key Concepts
- Core Data entity modeling and persistence
- SwiftUI reactive data flow with `@FetchRequest`
- Codable JSON serialization and file I/O
- CryptoKit AES-GCM symmetric encryption
- Secure storage for encryption keys (Keychain)
- Unit testing for persistence, encoding, and encryption

## Code Example
```swift
struct Entry: Codable {
    let id: UUID
    let timestamp: Date
    let mood: Int16
    let text: String
}

class EntryStore: ObservableObject {
    @Published var entries: [Entry] = []

    func exportToEncryptedJSON(key: SymmetricKey) throws -> URL {
        let encoder = JSONEncoder()
        encoder.dateEncodingStrategy = .iso8601
        let data = try encoder.encode(entries)
        let sealedBox = try AES.GCM.seal(data, using: key)
        let encryptedData = sealedBox.combined!
        let url = FileManager.default.urls(for: .documentDirectory, in: .userDomainMask)[0]
            .appendingPathComponent("mood_export.enc")
        try encryptedData.write(to: url)
        return url
    }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a robust, real-time data layer that stays responsive under network variability, using concurrency primitives and local caching.

## Key Concepts

- Swift concurrency with async/await and TaskGroups
- Local cache using SQLite
- Delta-based merge with per-item versioning
- Conflict resolution and ordering guarantees
- Test strategy for latency, reordering, and memory pressure

## Code Example

```swift
struct Post { let id: String; var version: Int; var content: String }
struct Delta { let id: String; let version: Int; let content: String }

func merge(_ deltas: [Delta], into cache: inout [String: Post]) -> [Post] {
  for d in deltas {
    if var existing = cache[d.id] {
      if d.version > existing.version {
        existing.version = d.version
        existing.content = d.content
        cache[d.id] = existing
      }
    } else {
      cache[d.id] = Post(id: d.id, version: d.version, content: d.content)
    }
  }
  return Array(cache.values)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and mitigate race conditions in the delta merge?
- How would you extend to multi-device sync and server-driven conflict resolution?

